<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Release 264 rejects compactLayoutAssignment on TransactionJournal. The deploy
  fails with CustomObject TransactionJournal → "invalid parameter value" for ANY
  value, including the platform default SYSTEM, so this is not a name-resolution
  problem: the field is simply not accepted on this object.

  Verified on a fresh 264 org by isolating the component. post_ux deploys clean
  with this element removed, and fails with it present even when
  RLM_Transaction_Journal_Compact_Layout already exists in the org, so it is not
  a same-transaction ordering problem either. Asset, Contract and Quote keep
  their assignments; they deploy fine, so this is TransactionJournal-specific.

  The compact layout itself still deploys and is retained; it is simply not the
  assigned default for the highlights panel. Account's billing compact layout is
  already shipped unassigned, so this matches existing behavior in this bundle.

  Do not re-add compactLayoutAssignment here without re-testing on a fresh 264
  org. It will fail the whole assemble_and_deploy_ux step.

  Why keep a file whose CustomObject element is now empty: it is functionally
  inert and deliberately so. Converting the assembled object directory with and
  without this file produces byte-identical metadata output and an identical
  package.xml, so the sibling compactLayout does not depend on it. The file is
  retained only because this is the path someone would open before re-adding the
  assignment, and it is the one place the warning above will actually be read.
  Deleting it costs nothing at deploy time and loses the warning.
-->
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
</CustomObject>
